<title>USA: Essef's plant closing cuts about 150 jobs.</title>
<headline>Essef's plant closing cuts about 150 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>CHARDON, Ohio 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Essef Corp spokesman said Wednesday the closing its Pac-Fab plant in City of Industry, Calif., will cost about 150 to 160 jobs.</p>
<p>The spokesman said the plant, which manafactures swimming pool equipment, employs about 180 people. He added the company will offer 20 to 30 the opportunity to continue working for the company.</p>
<p>Essef earlier today said it would take a $2.3 million charge, or $0.35 a share, in the quarter ending September 30 to pay for the plant closure.</p>
</text>
